# EC2 Instance Setup

## Instance Configuration

- AMI: Amazon Linux
- Instance Type: t3.micro
- Storage: 8GB gp3
- Connection Method: EC2 Instance Connect (Browser-based SSH)

## Why t3.micro?

Burstable performance instance suitable for learning and lightweight workloads.

## Security Group Configuration

- Port 22 (SSH)
- Port 80 (HTTP)
- Port 8080 (Application Testing)

## Key Learnings

- EC2 is a virtual machine running in AWS data centers.
- Each instance has private and public IP.
- Security Groups act as virtual firewalls.
- Avoid logging in as root for security reasons.